By the time you've levelled up enough to do the quest, you should have
explored enough leprechaun halls and treasure zoos to have bought
protection the ordinary way.

As far as getting weaker monsters goes, that only applies to randomly
generated monsters, and it's only partially determined by character
level. Let's say you're level 3 and on level 47 in Gehennom:
(3 + 47) / 2 = 25. You'll be encountering difficulty level 25 monsters
with your level 3 character. And the best AC boost you could
reasonably expect is 11 points (of which, as I mentioned earlier, you
could normally expect to get about 9).

Keeping character level low (as in, really low) is IMO an overrated
tactic. It's certainly not a whole-game strategy.
